  "summary": "Battalion Wars is Kuju London's action and real-time tactics game, first released for GameCube in North America on 19 September 2005.",
  "body": [
    "Battalion Wars is Kuju London's action and real-time tactics game, first released for GameCube in North America on 19 September 2005. The player directly controls a soldier or vehicle while commanding the rest of a small army. Infantry, tanks and aircraft share missions across a brightly caricatured military world. The campaign begins with a conflict between rival nations before a new threat changes their alliances. Its central challenge is practical: take part in the fighting without losing track of what the other units need to accomplish.",
    "Orders can address the whole battalion, one type of unit or an individual soldier. A group might follow the controlled character, defend a position or attack a selected target. Different weapons are suited to different opponents, so sending everyone into the same fight can waste valuable support. Switching directly into another unit changes the player's immediate role. A tank can confront armour while infantry secure a location, making the choice of who to control another part of arranging the wider force.",
    "Mission results measure destroyed enemies, surviving allies and completion time. Moving quickly is useful only if the battalion remains strong enough to finish the objective. Cover helps protect infantry, while supplies dropped during combat can restore soldiers or repair vehicles. The game connects tactical planning to the visible condition of the force accompanying the player. A successful advance is therefore more than reaching the destination: the surviving units show how carefully the commander's decisions protected the people and equipment needed along the way."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Command from inside the battle",
    "Send the right unit towards the next threat",
    "Bring the battalion home"
  ],
